# Lesson 10: One Word Substitutions

## Important One Word Substitutions List

| Term | English Definition | Hindi Meaning |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Ambidextrous** | One who can use either hand with ease | दोनों हाथों से काम करने में कुशल |
| **Anarchism / Anarchist** | One out to destroy all government, peace, and order | अराजकतावादी |
| **Apostate** | A person who has changed his faith | स्वधर्मत्यागी |
| **Arbitrator** | A person appointed by two parties to settle a dispute | मध्यस्थ / बिचौलिया |
| **Ascetic** | One who leads an austere life | सन्यासी |
| **Atheist** | A person who does not believe in God | नास्तिक |
| **Bankrupt / Insolvent**| One who is unable to pay his debts | दिवालिया / कंगाल |
| **Bigot / Fanatic** | One filled with excessive religious enthusiasm | कट्टरपंथी |
| **Bohemian** | An unconventional style of living | रूढ़िमुक्त व्यक्ति |
| **Cacographist** | One who is bad in spelling | अशुद्ध लिखने वाला |
| **Cannibal** | One who feeds on human flesh | नरभक्षी |
| **Carnivorous** | One who feeds on flesh/animals | मांसाहारी |
| **Connoisseur** | A critical judge of art and craft | कला / पाक का पारखी |
| **Contemporaries** | Persons living at the same time | समकालीन |
| **Convalescent** | One recovering from illness | स्वास्थ्य-लाभ पाने वाला |
| **Emigrant** | One who leaves his country to settle in another | देशत्यागी / प्रवासी |
| **Immigrant** | One who comes into a country to settle | आप्रवासी |
| **Fastidious** | Very selective in habits; hard to please | जिद्दी / दुराराध्य |
| **Fatalist** | One who believes in fate | भाग्यवादी |
| **Fugitive** | One who runs away from justice | भगोड़ा |
| **Gourmet / Gourmand** | A lover and connoisseur of good food | पेटू / स्वादिष्ट भोजन का पारखी |
| **Henpecked** | A husband ruled by his wife | जोरू का गुलाम |
| **Honorary** | Holding a post without any salary | अवैतनic |
| **Iconoclast** | Breaker of images and traditional beliefs | मूर्तिभंजक |
| **Pedestrian** | One who walks on foot | पैदल यात्री |
| **Sadist** | A person who derives pleasure from hurting others | परपीड़क |
| **Philatelist** | One who collects stamps | डाक टिकट संग्रहकर्ता |

---

## Vocabulary Key Words & Synonyms

* **Valour:** Bravery, Chivalry, Gallantry (साहस)
* **Volatile:** Changing, Temporal, Wavering (अस्थिर)
* **Stern:** Rigid, Harsh (कठोर)
* **Squalid:** Dirty, Filthy, Polluted (मैला/गंदा)
* **Spurious:** Counterfeit, Fake (नकली)
* **Sanguine:** Hopeful, Optimistic (आशावादी)
* **Rapid:** Fast, Swift (शीघ्र)
* **Reveal:** Disclose, Expose (राज खोलना)
* **Peril:** Danger, Jeopardy (संकट)
* **Placid:** Tranquil, Calm, Peaceful (शांत)
* **Obstinate:** Stubborn, Resolute (जिद्दी)
* **Novice:** Beginner, Tyro, Fresher (नौसिखिया)
* **Nimble:** Brisk, Agile (फुर्तीला)
* **Mitigate:** Alleviate, Lessen, Assuage (कम करना)
